            <ArticleTitle>Imipramine binding in depressed patients with psychogenic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Imipramine binding to platelet membranes from depressed patients was analyzed. The patients were divided into two groups: one with depression alone, another with depression and psychogenic pain. The depressed patients with psychogenic pain had lower imipramine binding than the depressed patients without pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
